# The oracle, and the gate that enforces it.
#
# ENVIRONMENT.md: humans decide what is built and what "correct" means. For this repo,
# "correct" is these files: the cedar goldens, the database and images they came from,
# the tests that compare against them, and the CI that runs those tests. A change here
# can make a broken product look green without touching a line of product code, so it
# needs the human who owns "correct" — not only green CI.
#
# The list is longer than the test files on purpose. A required check is just a name,
# and each of these decides what runs under it: the workflow (an edit to `run: true`
# keeps the name and passes), the scripts it calls, any Cargo.toml (a [[test]] entry
# can point a test name at another file), build scripts (they run before the tests
# compile), cargo config (a `runner` wraps every test binary) and the toolchain pin.
# Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are critical paths in ENVIRONMENT.md already.
#
# Enforced only once main requires review from code owners, with stale approvals
# dismissed on new pushes. Until then GitHub only requests a review, and not even that
# on a PR the owner opened.

/reference-solutions/                           @bryantharpe
/crates/*/tests/data/                           @bryantharpe
/fixtures/                                      @bryantharpe
/.secretsignore                                 @bryantharpe
/crates/plate-solver/tests/reference_parity.rs  @bryantharpe
/crates/plate-solver/tests/image_parity.rs      @bryantharpe
/crates/grpc-service/tests/e2e_service.rs       @bryantharpe
/crates/star-detection/tests/parity.rs          @bryantharpe
/scripts/ci/                                    @bryantharpe
/.github/                                       @bryantharpe
Cargo.toml                                      @bryantharpe
/Cargo.lock                                     @bryantharpe
build.rs                                        @bryantharpe
/.cargo/                                        @bryantharpe
/rust-toolchain*                                @bryantharpe
